        "modelingNotes": [
          "Manufacturer spelling LC1D80BD; requested LC1-D80BD retains the historical presentation hyphen. Exact sheet confirms the remaining code and historical description; no successor substitution.",
          "Coil has no built-in suppressor (p. 3). The simplified circuit diagram omits polarity signs; Schneider FAQFA121938 for LC1D***D DC coils requires A1 positive and A2 negative (https://www.se.com/us/en/faqs/FA121938/, published2007-08-28,modified2026-05-12). This explicit instruction governs the modeled coil polarity.",
          "AC-3 80 A and AC-1 125 A at <=440 V AC and <=60 °C; 37 kW at 380–400 V AC 50/60 Hz AC-3. Coil consumption 22 W at 20 °C. Conditional contact capabilities are not assigned as scalar ratings.",
          "Keys preserve diagram markings, including 13/NO and 21/NC. Mechanical actuation, coil impedance and normally closed contact state do not join nets; no fixed links are asserted.",
          "A1 and A2 are required for coil operation. Passive main and auxiliary contact connections depend on application. Optional add-on contacts and suppressors are excluded.",
          "No PE, shield or communication connection is documented. Duplicate physical coil-access locations and any corresponding links are unverified; no additional terminals or links are inferred."
